  "factual_review": [
    {
      "assessment": "Copied qualified metadata records reward 1, admitted native completion and zero remaining processes/zero worker cleanup for each arm. README does not assign correctness or settlement authority to the acknowledgment.",
      "claim": "Native outcomes and lifecycle",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "assessment": "One planning and one coding session per fresh arm, same ordinary reply contract/model/CLI/reasoning/resource/cache/task/source/archive controls and zero retries are consistent with qualification/preflight. Native cumulative usage includes complete sessions, not merely initial task-prompt bytes.",
      "claim": "Preserved planning/coding and declared controls",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "assessment": "59,731 versus 57,160 complete coding bytes and 62,443 versus 61,172 native bytes match results. README explicitly attributes part of byte variation to different generated plans and declines single-pair causal/repeatable savings. Six/eight native counter records remain observations, not API calls.",
      "claim": "Byte differences and stochastic plans",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "assessment": "Cached input and reasoning subcategories are included in input/output totals. All seven retained attempts and 13 sessions sum to the stated campaign cost; its scope excludes unrelated project/model/training runs.",
      "claim": "Accounting interpretation",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "assessment": "Initial pair remains unqualified despite both rewards 1. Its 659,361-token cost and lost-provider InvalidReceipt are preserved; source fix/test qualification does not retroactively reconstruct deleted context or replace old native audits.",
      "claim": "Historical audit failure retained",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "assessment": "Copied author qualification and independent review bind conditional provider propagation and 37 reported passing tests with actual subprocess coverage. Missing/foreign values and legacy/null IPC remain strict. Tests are authored offline evidence, not new benchmark/provider results.",
      "claim": "IPC fix qualification",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "assessment": "README expressly includes worker/lifecycle/custody work in R4 and states paired arms use that same snapshot; it does not widen the scoped 29-file only-IPC rebase claim into whole-runtime equivalence.",
      "claim": "Concurrent runtime scope",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "assessment": "P0 remains a proposed opt-in acceptance reference with exact reconstruction and new independent planning-input audit required; coding share 89.78% is prioritization, not savings. Generic owner gateway remains unqualified; embeddings only nominate. Six native verdicts, fresh completeness/closure and no metadata omission authority are retained.",
      "claim": "Future improvement backlog",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "assessment": "The copied revision 3 backlog/review accurately label compact pending at their plan revision. Final README uses completed qualified result metadata and does not present the snapshot as a final arm result.",
      "claim": "Dated backlog snapshot and final result",
      "passed": true
    }
  ],
